# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit.primitives\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qiskit.primitives\"></span>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "qiskit.primitives {#qiskitprimitives}"
msgstr "qiskit.primitives {#qiskitprimitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most notable change in the [`qiskit.primitives`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/primitives) module is the\n"
"introduction of the new **primitives V2 interface**. This section shows how to migrate your\n"
"workflow from primitives V1 to primitives V2, as well as the few changes that have taken place\n"
"in the inputs accepted by the V1 interface.\n"
msgstr ""
"Najbardziej znaczącą zmianą w module [`qiskit.primitives`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/primitives) jest\n"
"wprowadzenie nowego **interfejsu prymitywów V2**. Ta sekcja pokazuje, jak przenieść swój\n"
"przepływ pracy z prymitywów V1 do prymitywów V2, a także nieliczne zmiany, które zaszły\n"
"w danych wejściowych akceptowanych przez interfejs V1.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Starting with the v1.0 release, we will refer to the pre-1.0 primitives interface as \"primitives V1\".\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Począwszy od wersji v1.0, będziemy odnosić się do interfejsu prymitywów sprzed wersji 1.0 jako „prymitywy V1\".\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"migrate-to-v2\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"migrate-to-v2\"></span>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from V1 to V2 {#migrate-from-v1-to-v2}"
msgstr "Migracja z V1 do V2 {#migrate-from-v1-to-v2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The formal distinction between the primitives V1 and V2 APIs are the base classes from which\n"
"primitives implementations inherit. To transition to the new base classes, you can maintain\n"
"the original import path from `qiskit.primitives`:\n"
msgstr ""
"Formalne rozróżnienie między API prymitywów V1 i V2 wynika z klas bazowych, "
"po których dziedziczą implementacje prymitywów. Aby przejść na nowe klasy "
"bazowe, możesz zachować oryginalną ścieżkę importu z `qiskit.primitives`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from                     |   Replace with\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`BaseEstimator`         |  [`BaseEstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseEstimatorV2)\n"
"`BaseSampler`             |  [`BaseSamplerV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseSamplerV2)\n"
msgstr ""
"Migruj z                     |   Zamień na\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`BaseEstimator`         |  [`BaseEstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseEstimatorV2)\n"
"`BaseSampler`             |  [`BaseSamplerV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseSamplerV2)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The names of the qiskit core implementations of the V2 primitives (those importable from `qiskit.primitives`),\n"
"have been modified to clarify their purpose as implementations that can be run locally\n"
"with a statevector simulator backend. The new names **do not include the -V2 suffix**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nazwy implementacji prymitywów V2 w rdzeniu qiskit (tych importowalnych z `qiskit.primitives`)\n"
"zostały zmienione, aby lepiej oddać ich przeznaczenie jako implementacji, które można uruchamiać lokalnie\n"
"z backendem symulatora wektorów stanu. Nowe nazwy **nie zawierają sufiksu -V2**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from                     |   Replace with\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Estimator`         |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator)\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Sampler`             |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler)\n"
msgstr ""
"Migruj z                     |   Zamień na\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Estimator`         |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator)\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Sampler`             |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are some conceptual differences to think about when migrating from V1 to V2.\n"
"These differences are dictated by the base class, but are shown in the following examples using the statevector\n"
"implementations found in `qiskit.primitives`:\n"
msgstr ""
"Podczas migracji z V1 do V2 warto wziąć pod uwagę pewne różnice koncepcyjne.\n"
"Wynikają one z klasy bazowej, ale zostały pokazane w poniższych przykładach z użyciem implementacji opartych na wektorach stanu\n"
"dostępnych w `qiskit.primitives`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the following examples, assume the following imports and primitive "
"initializations:\n"
msgstr ""
"W poniższych przykładach przyjmij następujące importy i inicjalizacje "
"prymitywów:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. `Sampler and Estimator`: The new V2 primitives are designed to accept **vectorized inputs**, where single circuits can be grouped with array-valued specifications. That is, one circuit can be executed\n"
"  for arrays of `n` parameter sets, `n` observables, or both (in the case of Estimator). Each group is called a **primitive unified bloc (pub)**, and can be represented as a tuple: `(1 x circuit, [n x observables], [n x parameters])`. The V1 interface didn't allow for the same flexibility.  Instead, the number of input circuits had to match the number of observables and\n"
"  parameter sets, as shown in the following examples (select a tab to see each example):\n"
msgstr ""
"1. `Sampler i Estimator`: Nowe prymitywy V2 są zaprojektowane do przyjmowania **wektoryzowanych danych wejściowych**, gdzie pojedyncze Circuit mogą być grupowane ze specyfikacjami w postaci tablic. Oznacza to, że jeden obwód może być wykonany\n"
"  dla tablic `n` zestawów parametrów, `n` obserwabli lub obu jednocześnie (w przypadku Estimator). Każda taka grupa nazywana jest **primitive unified bloc (PUB)** i może być reprezentowana jako krotka: `(1 x Circuit, [n x obserwable], [n x parametry])`. Interfejs V1 nie pozwalał na taką samą elastyczność. Zamiast tego liczba wejściowych Circuitów musiała odpowiadać liczbie obserwabli i\n"
"  zestawów parametrów, co pokazują poniższe przykłady (wybierz zakładkę, aby zobaczyć każdy z nich):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables\" default>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables\" default>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 4, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 4, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-1-3\" label=\"Sampler, 1 circuit, 3 parameter sets\" default>\n"
msgstr ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-1-3\" label=\"Sampler, 1 circuit, 3 parameter sets\" default>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit] * 3, [vals1, vals2, vals3])\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit] * 3, [vals1, vals2, vals3])\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V2\n"
"      job = sampler_v2.run([(circuit, [vals1, vals2, vals3])])\n"
"      counts = job.result()[0].data.meas.get_counts()\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4-2\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables, 2 parameter sets\" default>\n"
msgstr ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V2\n"
"      job = sampler_v2.run([(circuit, [vals1, vals2, vals3])])\n"
"      counts = job.result()[0].data.meas.get_counts()\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4-2\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables, 2 parameter sets\" default>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 8, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4] * 2, [vals1, vals2] * 4)\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 8, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4] * 2, [vals1, vals2] * 4)\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [[obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4]], [[vals1], [vals2]])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [[obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4]], [[vals1], [vals2]])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  V2 primitives accept multiple PUBs as inputs, and each pub gets its own result. This\n"
"  lets you run different circuits with various parameter/observable combinations,\n"
"  which was not always possible in the V1 interface:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Prymitywy V2 przyjmują wiele PUBów jako dane wejściowe, a każdy PUB otrzymuje własny wynik. Pozwala to\n"
"  uruchamiać różne Circuity z różnymi kombinacjami parametrów i obserwabli,\n"
"  co nie zawsze było możliwe w interfejsie V1:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-2-1\" label=\"Sampler, 2 circuits, 1 parameter set\" default>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-2-1\" label=\"Sampler, 2 circuits, 1 parameter set\" default>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 2 circuits with 1 parameter set using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit1, circuit2], [vals1] * 2)\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 2 circuits with 1 parameter set using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit1, circuit2], [vals1] * 2)\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 2 circuits with 1 parameter set using Sampler V2\n"
